(ned -- helper for cal_c_zero. ONE SUB PER FILE: LinuxCNC resolves)
(subroutines through SUBROUTINE_PATH, and a second sub defined in)
(the calling file is NOT found -- "EOF in file ... seeking o-word",)
(reproduced offline with rs274. Shared setup arrives in GLOBAL)
(parameters; the result goes back the same way.)
(===================== helper: ONE probe toward centre =====================)
(#1 = A tilt angle, #2 = Y offset off centre. Returns #<_cc_tx>.)
o<cc_probe> sub
  #<ang>  = #1
  #<yoff> = #2

  (clear BEFORE any A move, then tilt, then line up)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<_cc_top> + #<_cc_safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
  G1 A#<ang> F[#<_cc_frot>]
  G1 X#<_cc_xr> Y[#<_cc_cy> + #<yoff>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]

  (protective descent to the probing height -- never plunge blind)
  G91
  G38.3 Z-[#<_cc_safe> + #<_cc_zoff>] F[#<_cc_fck>]
  o205 if [#5070 EQ 1]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<_cc_top> + #<_cc_safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL C: contact while descending - the standoff is over the puck, not in front of it. Re-teach with SET C REF.)
  o205 endif

  (drive toward the puck centre in +X)
  G38.3 X#<_cc_reach> F[#<_cc_fpr>]
  o210 if [#5070 EQ 0]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<_cc_top> + #<_cc_safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL C: no contact driving toward centre - the tip is not lined up with the puck. Re-teach with SET C REF.)
  o210 endif
  G1 X-[#<_cc_back>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
  G38.2 X[#<_cc_back> + 1] F[#<_cc_fla>]
  #<_cc_tx> = #5061

  (RELEASE PROVEN, NOT GUESSED. G38.5 backs off until the probe OPENS and)
  (stops there -- "probe until no contact away from work, no error", the form)
  (used by stock rectangle_probe.ngc. A blind G1 of a guessed distance can)
  (leave the rod still touching, and then the FIRST non-probe move of the)
  (NEXT cycle dies with "probe tripped during non-probe move" -- one abort)
  (poisoning every run after it, which is what happened 2026-08-03. This is)
  (not a contact-quality question: it is about never issuing an ordinary move)
  (while the probe is made.)
  G38.5 X-[2 * #<_cc_back>] F[#<_cc_fla>]
  G1 X-[#<_cc_back>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
  G90
  G1 Z[#<_cc_top> + #<_cc_safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
o<cc_probe> endsub

M2 (end helper)
